<title>SLOVENIA: Shell Slovenia to open first petrol station in May.</title>
<headline>Shell Slovenia to open first petrol station in May.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Slovenija, a subsidiary of Royal Dutch Shell Group, said on Tuesday it planned to open its first petrol station in Slovenia in May.</p>
<p>The station, in the norther city of Jesenice 10 kms (6 miles) from the Austrian border, will be the first of four petrol stations the company said it planned to open over the course of the year, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Shell's new station will be the company's first in the area of the former Yugoslavia, from which Slovenia gained independence in 1991.</p>
<p>-- Marja Novak, Ljubljana Newsroom, 386-61-126-3644</p>
